    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Home to Grow Into, A Lifestyle to Love in the Heart of Dunhill.\r\n\r\nSome homes are simply about bricks and mortar. Others offer something more. A sense of place, space to breathe and the opportunity to create a life surrounded by nature, community and the people who matter most.\r\n\r\nComing to the market for the very first time, this substantial five bedroom detached bungalow has been lovingly maintained by its current owner for over 20 years. Set on a beautiful mature site in the picturesque village of Dunhill, it is a home that has been genuinely cared for and enjoyed, and now presents a wonderful opportunity for its next owners to make it their own.\r\n\r\nFor families, the location is particularly special. The local school is literally around the corner, bringing a wonderful ease to everyday life, while the scenic Anne Valley Walk is just down the road. Whether it is an early morning walk, an evening stroll or simply enjoying the changing seasons, having such a beautiful natural amenity so close to home is a real privilege.\r\n\r\nDunhill itself offers the kind of lifestyle that is increasingly difficult to find. A peaceful village setting, a strong sense of community and beautiful countryside, with the spectacular Waterford coast also within easy reach. It is a place where children can grow up surrounded by space and nature, where weekends can be spent exploring nearby beaches and coastal villages, and where coming home at the end of the day feels like leaving the rush behind.\r\nThe property is approached through a double entrance driveway, providing generous parking and an attractive sense of arrival. The mature grounds are an integral part of the home's appeal, with established trees and native hedgerow to the rear creating a wonderfully natural and settled backdrop.\r\nThere is plenty of outdoor space for children to play, for gardening enthusiasts to make their mark or simply for enjoying long summer evenings at home. The generous site, which is approximately 0.47 acres, also offers ample scope for the addition of a garage, subject to the necessary planning permission.\r\n\r\nStep inside and the sense of space is immediately apparent. A generous entrance hallway welcomes you into the home and provides access to the principal living accommodation.\r\n\r\nTo the left is a large reception room, a warm and comfortable space centred around a stove. It is perfect for quiet evenings, family gatherings or simply settling in on a winter's night. To the right of the hallway is a separate formal dining room, offering a dedicated space for family dinners, celebrations and entertaining.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the home is the spacious kitchen diner, designed for everyday family life and featuring a beautiful mosaic style splashback that adds character and personality to the space. There is ample room for dining, conversation and the daily rhythm of family life, from busy weekday mornings to long, relaxed weekend breakfasts.\r\n\r\nA separate utility room provides valuable practicality, while an adjoining WC with shower adds further convenience for a busy household.\r\nThe bedroom accommodation is particularly generous, with five bedrooms and four bathrooms in total. The principal bedroom benefits from its own ensuite, while a further bedroom also enjoys direct access to an ensuite.\r\n\r\nThe flexibility of five bedrooms opens up a world of possibilities. There is space for a growing family, visiting guests, a home office, a hobby room or comfortable accommodation for extended family. It is a home capable of adapting as life changes over the years.\r\n\r\nOil fired central heating serves the property, which has been carefully and lovingly maintained throughout its ownership.\r\n\r\nWhat makes this home particularly appealing is the combination of space, setting and lifestyle. You can step outside and be surrounded by mature greenery, walk to the local school in moments, head down the road to the beautiful Anne Valley Walk or explore the nearby Waterford coast.\r\n\r\nFor over two decades, this has been a much loved home. Now, as it comes to the market for the very first time, it offers someone new the opportunity to begin their own chapter here.\r\n\r\nA home with space to grow, room to gather and a setting to fall in love with, right in the heart of Dunhill village. \r\n\r\nGuide Price €435,000\r\n\r\nViewings are by appointment only."
      },
